      <section class="svetlina-section" aria-label="Methodology and Verification">
        <div class="svetlina-section-head">
          <h2>5. Methodology, Presumption of Innocence &amp; Cryptographic Verification</h2>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size:0.86rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink, #0f172a);">
          <p>
            <strong>Exact Binomial Model &amp; BH FDR:</strong> Within every stratum (<code>court × department × case type × year</code>), each judge&apos;s baseline allocation share <code>s_j</code> is measured directly from assigned cases. Parties representing &gt;40% of a stratum are excluded as structural monopolists. One-sided exact binomial probabilities <code>P(X ≥ k | n_P, s_j)</code> are corrected across all {fmtIntEn(testsRun)} tests via Benjamini–Hochberg FDR. RED flags satisfy <code>q &lt; 0.01</code>, <code>k ≥ 5</code>, and <code>ratio ≥ 3.0</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Legal Disclaimer &amp; GDPR:</strong> Red/Amber indicators are <em>purely statistical triage signals</em> warranting institutional inspection under Art. 9 of the Bulgarian Judiciary Act (random case allocation); they do not assert guilt or unlawful conduct. Automated ingress filtering excludes all natural persons, personal identification numbers (EGN), and sensitive health records.
          </p>
          <p class="mono" style="font-size:0.78rem;word-break:break-all;">
            <strong>Raw File SHA-256 (Zenodo &amp; Live JSON):</strong> b6a49ec4644042f43657c10d413e5d055cb3f1e04b57fa3595565999fdec2bc3<br />
            <strong>Canonical RED Snapshot SHA-256:</strong> {SHA256_SNAPSHOT}<br />
            <strong>CERN Zenodo Permanent Archive:</strong> <a href={ZENODO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://doi.org/{ZENODO_DOI}</a>
          </p>
          <div class="svet-wasm-card" id="svetWasmVerifierCard">
            <div class="svet-wasm-top">
